Version 2.4.1 is a small update to the previous version, fixing a bug
in the rendering of the OscSpread parameter, parallel builds,
as well the MacOS Github workflow.

Fixes:
- The OscSpread parameter had a much smaller effect than intended,
  since version 2.2.0 . It has now been fixed so it has the same range as
  before. Apologies for any user patches made than now have too much
  oscillator spread.
- Parallel builds (make -j 3 is used by Zynthian upstream builds) failed
  (only the DPF framework was built) due to incorrect dependencies.
  This has been corrected.
- Github updated their MacOS build support, causing the upstream build to
  fail. This has been rectified. This doesn't affect the plugin itself nor
  the Linux builds.

Other changes:
- Minor optimization in the LCT/LCR portamento code to bring the CPU load
  down to the same level as for exponential portamento. The difference is
  very small (about 0.5% CPU with 32 voices playing, oversampling enabled,
  on an RPi5).

As usual, a companion version 2.4.1z has been tagged on the Zynthian branch,
which supports the graphic envelope and filter display features in the Zynthian
UI.
